      "message": "We should create a `struct` to hold `vid` and `pid` together.\n\n----\n\n\n### Rationale\n\nRefactoring the loose `vid` and `pid` variables into a cohesive `UsbDeviceId` struct brings several significant architectural improvements:\n\n1. **Prevents \"Primitive Obsession\" \u0026 Accidental Swaps:** When APIs accept multiple parameters of the same primitive type (e.g., `Initialize(uint16_t vid, uint16_t pid)`), the compiler cannot prevent you from accidentally passing `Initialize(pid, vid)`. Wrapping them in a struct enforces compile-time type safety.\n2. **Self-Documenting Code:** Leveraging C++20 designated initializers (`{.vid \u003d ..., .pid \u003d ...}`) explicitly documents the intent at the call site and initialization points.\n3. **Value Semantics:** A VID/PID pair represents a single logical identity. Adding a C++20 defaulted `\u003d\u003d` operator allows the struct to be treated as a strict value type.\n4. **Testability:** Google Mock requires arguments to be equality-comparable to match them in `EXPECT_CALL`. Furthermore, `EXPECT_EQ` can now assert against the entire struct at once, rather than requiring line-by-line checks for `vid` and `pid`.\n\n---\n\n### Required Changes\n\nHere are the step-by-step updates needed across the codebase to implement this:\n\n#### 1. Define the Struct \u0026 Update Base Interfaces\n\n**File: `util/elan/usb_backend.h**`\n\n```cpp\n// 1. Add the struct definition above the UsbBackend class\nstruct UsbDeviceId {\n  uint16_t vid;\n  uint16_t pid;\n\n  // C++20 auto-generates the member-wise comparison\n  bool operator\u003d\u003d(const UsbDeviceId\u0026) const \u003d default;\n};\n\nclass UsbBackend {\n public:\n  virtual ~UsbBackend() \u003d default;\n\n  virtual int Initialize() \u003d 0;\n  // 2. Refactor OpenDevice\n  virtual int OpenDevice(UsbDeviceId device_id) \u003d 0; \n  // ...\n};\n\n```\n\n#### 2. Update Constants and Controller API\n\n**File: `util/elan/iap_control.h**`\n\n```cpp\n// 1. Replace the separate constants\nconstexpr UsbDeviceId kBootDevice \u003d {.vid \u003d 0x04F3, .pid \u003d 0x0910};\n\nclass IapControl {\n public:\n  // ...\n  // 2. Update signature\n  [[nodiscard]] std::expected\u003cvoid, IapError\u003e Initialize(UsbDeviceId device_id);\n\n```\n\n**File: `util/elan/iap_control.cc**`\n\n```cpp\nstd::expected\u003cvoid, IapError\u003e IapControl::Initialize(UsbDeviceId device_id) {\n  if (int err \u003d usb_-\u003eInitialize(); err !\u003d 0) {\n    return std::unexpected(IapError::UsbInitFailed);\n  }\n  // Pass the struct directly down to the backend\n  if (int err \u003d usb_-\u003eOpenDevice(device_id); err !\u003d 0) {\n    return std::unexpected(IapError::DeviceNotFound);\n  }\n  return {};\n}\n\n```\n\n#### 3. Update the USB Implementations\n\n**File: `util/elan/libusb_backend.h**`\n\n```cpp\n  int OpenDevice(UsbDeviceId device_id) override;\n\n```\n\n**File: `util/elan/libusb_backend.cc**`\n\n```cpp\nint LibusbBackend::OpenDevice(UsbDeviceId device_id) {\n// ... inside the descriptor loop:\n      if (desc.idVendor \u003d\u003d device_id.vid \u0026\u0026 desc.idProduct \u003d\u003d device_id.pid) {\n        found_dev \u003d list.get()[i];\n        break;\n      }\n\n```\n\n**File: `util/elan/fake_usb_backend.h**`\n\n```cpp\n  int OpenDevice(UsbDeviceId device_id) override { return 0; }\n\n```\n\n**File: `util/elan/mock_usb_backend.h**`\n\n```cpp\n  MOCK_METHOD(int, OpenDevice, (UsbDeviceId device_id), (override));\n\n```\n\n#### 4. Update the CLI State\n\n**File: `util/elan/cli.h**`\n\n```cpp\nstruct CmdLine {\n  UsbDeviceId device_id; // Replaces vid and pid\n  std::string file_path;\n  bool show_help \u003d false;\n};\n\n```\n\n**File: `util/elan/cli.cc**`\n\n```cpp\nstd::optional\u003cCmdLine\u003e ParseCommandLine(int argc, char* argv[]) {\n  // Use designated initializers for clean default state\n  CmdLine cmd{\n      .device_id \u003d kBootDevice,\n      .file_path \u003d \"\",\n      .show_help \u003d false\n  };\n\n  // ..